.page break 1 leave or restart a loop
.alias continue

# SYNOPSIS
*break* [_N_]
*continue* [_N_]

# DESCRIPTION
These gapsh builtins work inside `for`, `while` and `until` loops. `break` ends the loop; `continue` skips to the next round. With _N_ they act on the _N_th enclosing loop.

# EXAMPLES
    for f in *; do [ -d "$f" ] && continue; echo "$f"; done
    while :; do read line || break; echo "got $line"; done

# SEE ALSO
gapsh-language(7), true(1)
